    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0361" n="47" xml:id="pg47"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.0055/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitlock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-06T17:00:00+00:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 6, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7:40 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Diplomatic corps convened for this evening to discuss subject of my August 5, 9
                    a.m. Care of Americans requires my constant attention. The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tennessee</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d105-f1"/> is about
                    to arrive at Ostend, therefore I feel that I can render more real service by
                    remaining here. I should like Department’s views.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitlock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d105-f1" n="1" xml:id="d105-f1-content">
                <p>Warship bringing gold for the relief of American citizens.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
